It calls the official Adax remote user client API
(https://adax.no/en/wi-fi/api-development/, OpenAPI document at
https://api-1.adax.no/client-api/openapi) with the account id and a credential
the user creates in the Adax WiFi app. Adax is a trademark of Adax AS (Glen
Dimplex Nordic); this integration is not affiliated with nor endorsed by Adax.

Protocol knowledge
------------------
The endpoints, the password grant, the hundredths of a degree and the
`?withEnergy=1` fields come from the official Adax documentation and its
OpenAPI document. The pace of one request every 30 seconds comes from pyAdax
by Daniel Hjelseth Høyer (https://github.com/Danielhiversen/pyAdax, MIT
License), the library of the Home Assistant "adax" component; the shape of
the energy values (a saw tooth that restarts at every hour) from the Home
Assistant issue home-assistant/core#150994. No code was copied from them:
this integration is an independent JavaScript implementation of the same API.
